## Phase 4 — Multi-Agent Orchestration Engine

### Goal
Execute workflows through the 5-agent chain with full lifecycle control (pause, resume, cancel).

---

### Backend

#### [NEW] `server/src/agents/plannerAgent.js`
Determines node execution order, emits confidence score, returns plan.

#### [NEW] `server/src/agents/executionAgent.js`
Runs each node against the correct integration or AI provider.

#### [NEW] `server/src/agents/validationAgent.js`
Verifies required output fields after each node.

#### [NEW] `server/src/agents/recoveryAgent.js`
Classifies failures: `MISSING_FIELDS | API_FAILURE | AUTH_EXPIRED | RATE_LIMIT | TRANSIENT` → decides `retry_with_backoff | escalate`.

#### [NEW] `server/src/agents/monitoringAgent.js`
Emits timeline events (ExecutionLog rows + Socket.IO events).

#### [NEW] `server/src/agents/orchestrator.js`
Chains all 5 agents. Reports `langGraph: 'available' | 'not-installed'`. Writes one `ExecutionLog` per agent event. Emits Socket.IO event per step. Manages `PAUSED` / `CANCELLED` state checks between nodes.

#### [NEW] `server/src/services/executionService.js`
create, getById, getTimeline, pause, resume, cancel — all persisted to `Execution` + `ExecutionLog` collections.

#### [NEW] `server/src/controllers/executionController.js`

#### [NEW] `server/src/routes/executionRoutes.js`
All 6 execution endpoints.

